Z||000000||Shaun41178||11-16-1999||06:31 PM||||I have thought about getting my pulley dyno tested.  I have had my car dyno tested before the pulley so a baseline has already been established.<P>However it costs $75 to have it dyno tested.  Now I don't feel the need to have it dyno tested but maybe some of you do before you buy it.  I can attest to that it does make your car quicker in the qtr mile.  But everyone likes to here dyno numbers.  So here is my thought.<P>Would anyone want to chip in like $1 or even less to put in a fund to help me pay for this dyno time?  I know it sounds korny and many will probably think that it is part of a way to get money and such.  But I assure you that the money will go to the "pulley dyno fund"  I will not except more then $75 total as that is the cost of the dyno time.  I also have no problem paying for part of it but I don't want to pay all $75 for it.<P>So is anyone interested in doing this? Any replys would be great even if all of you think it would be a bad idea then please respond.   If any think that it is a good idea then post as well.  I want to know what many of you think of an idea like this.<P>This money will not go to me buying a pulley as I already have one.  Like I said it will go towards the dyno time.<P>If any of you want to look at my webpage to see my baseline dyno runs then go to <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178</A> <BR>and then scroll down to Dyno runs or something like that.<P>Thanks||||reg||3
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||11-16-1999||07:56 PM||||Well I am thinking of buying the pully and a $1 investment seems much better than spending $80.00 and bloody knuckles to boot. I would like to know what the pulley yeilds....count me in.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Phil||11-16-1999||09:18 PM||||Go on the Power Tour next year ($25 entry fee)and you can go on the dyno for free.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||11-17-1999||02:00 PM||||$25 for a dyno run?  not bad considering I would have to compete with many otehr cars to get on the dyno and there just might not be enough time.  Besides I would have to wait till next summer to have the pulley tested.  Not what i had in mind.  I was thinking of something more in the lines of the next month.<P>Anyone else care to comment?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||11-17-1999||02:10 PM||||Actually the line to get on the dyno wasn't that long. I think a lot of people really didn't want to know their actual numbers. There were quite a few dissapointed owners, seems their claims of 300-400 HP didn't exactly pan out.I forget what your baseline was but isn't it amazing how much is lost going through the drivetrain. One guy clained 375 horse and wound up 215, he couldn't melt into the crowd fast enough.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||11-17-1999||04:03 PM||||Phil, you are correct! At least 98% of people that dyno their engines are pretty disappointed at the numbers.<P>Shaun, just a suggestion. Why not talk to the pulley company and explain what you want to do. Convince them it would be great advertising when you post your results to the Fiero community. Maybe they will spring for part of the bill or better yet, they might have access to one themselves that they'd let you use. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaun41178||11-18-1999||01:05 AM||||Batboy: Not a bad idea unfortunately that won't happen.  First I bought it from the Fiero Store and they aren't going to help with the bill for sure.  But even if the pulley was bought from a different co then they still would not ante up money to pay for part of the bill.  For one if the pulley did not make the power that was advertised then they would not want the tests to be posted.  They arn't going to shell out more money to find that there product does not produce power like they say it does.  Its a gamble but not one these relatively small companies are willing to take.<P>Ok people.  I am guessing that no one is responding to this post that most agree that it is a bad idea or is not willing to give up $1 or less to this fund.  Can I assume this?  Please just say whether you would do it or not or that it is a bad idea or not.  Or just say that it is a good idea but you still aren't going to give a bit of money.<P>I have one person behind me so far.  i guess it is a start but not the following like I thought it would get.||||reg||1
Z||000007||superXmotorsports||11-18-1999||08:52 PM||||I used the ASP pulley on my last 3.2L build. My friend at the machine shop said he would estimate 2-5hp max gain.  (I also eliminated the A/C too.)  I will sponsor you $20 if you display a 'Super X Motorsports' windshield decal on your car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
